  "description": "KAMNEU crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C96 H90 Ho6 N8 O26. From the CIF bond table, Ho1 (Ho) has 7 O neighbors; Ho2 (Ho) has 7 O neighbors; Ho3 (Ho) has 6 O neighbors; Ho1B (Ho) has 7 O neighbors; Ho2B (Ho) has 7 O neighbors; Ho3B (Ho) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 11 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.447-3.820 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 85.91-119.13°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C96H90Ho6N8O26. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
